@startuml DynamicPPMigrationArchitecture
title vLLM V1 Dynamic Pipeline-Parallel Reconfiguration Architecture

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

skinparam package {
  BackgroundColor<<upstream>> #EEF3FF
  BorderColor<<upstream>> #6B7FD7
  BackgroundColor<<extension>> #FFF4E6
  BorderColor<<extension>> #D9822B
  BackgroundColor<<runtime>> #EAF7EA
  BorderColor<<runtime>> #4E9A51
}

skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #555555
}

legend right
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  | <back:#EEF3FF>    </back> | Existing vLLM V1 execution structure |
  | <back:#FFF4E6>    </back> | Dynamic PP / migration extension |
  | <back:#EAF7EA>    </back> | Runtime state transfer and execution |
endlegend

package "Existing vLLM V1 structure" <<upstream>> {
  [V1 EngineCore] as UpstreamEngine
  [V1 Scheduler] as UpstreamScheduler
  [Ray Distributed Executor] as UpstreamExecutor
  [GPU Worker / ModelRunner] as UpstreamWorker
  [KV Cache] as KVCache

  UpstreamEngine --> UpstreamScheduler : schedule requests
  UpstreamEngine --> UpstreamExecutor : execute batches
  UpstreamExecutor --> UpstreamWorker : run model
  UpstreamWorker --> KVCache : read/write KV
}

package "Dynamic PP reconfiguration extension" <<extension>> {
  [DynamicConfig\n- pp layout\n- migration steps\n- autoscaling flags] as DynamicConfig
  [DynamicEngineCore\nRuntime layout manager] as DynamicEngine
  [DynamicScheduler\nSingle active PP layout] as DynamicScheduler
  [DynamicSchedulerOutput\nBatch-local PP layout\nMigration metadata] as DynamicOutput
  [DynamicRayDistributedExecutor\nRuntime PP routing\nNo compiled DAG] as DynamicExecutor
  [DynamicGPUWorker\nLayer assignment\nKV state transfer] as DynamicWorker
}

package "Runtime migration data plane" <<runtime>> {
  [Dynamic Model\nLayer assignment] as DynamicModel
  [KV Synchronizer\nKV patch send/apply] as KVSynchronizer
  [Runtime PP topology\nPer-batch active ranks] as PPRouting
}

DynamicConfig --> DynamicEngine : initial layout,\ntarget layouts,\ntrigger policy

DynamicEngine -up-|> UpstreamEngine
DynamicScheduler -up-|> UpstreamScheduler
DynamicExecutor -up-|> UpstreamExecutor
DynamicWorker -up-|> UpstreamWorker

DynamicEngine --> DynamicScheduler : current layout\npending target layout
DynamicScheduler --> DynamicOutput : scheduled batch +\npp_layer_config
DynamicOutput --> DynamicExecutor : execute with\nbatch-local layout
DynamicExecutor --> DynamicWorker : add/remove layers\nstart/finalize migration\nresize KV
DynamicWorker --> DynamicModel : change layer assignment
DynamicWorker --> KVSynchronizer : send/apply KV patches
KVSynchronizer --> KVCache : migrate KV state
DynamicExecutor --> PPRouting : activate/deactivate ranks\nroute PP messages
PPRouting --> DynamicWorker : forward batch through\nselected active ranks

DynamicWorker --> DynamicExecutor : applied tokens,\nall_patch_applied,\nresize_done
DynamicExecutor --> DynamicEngine : migration state
DynamicEngine --> DynamicScheduler : switch active layout\nat sync boundary

note right of DynamicEngine
Main external abstraction:

change_configuration(target_pp_layout)

This may be implemented with sync,
async, async_fast, or baseline strategy.
end note

note bottom of DynamicScheduler
Important structural choice:

The scheduler does not run two request queues.
It keeps one active PP layout.
The target layout is only a pending transition
until the sync boundary batch is emitted.
end note

note bottom of DynamicOutput
Each scheduled batch carries its own PP layout.
Old-layout batches can finish naturally.
New-layout batches start after the consistency boundary.
end note

note right of KVSynchronizer
Migration correctness depends on coordinating:

1. Layer assignment
2. KV state transfer

Changing layer assignment alone is not sufficient.
The corresponding KV state must move as well.
end note

note right of DynamicExecutor
This path intentionally does not use
a compiled DAG for PP execution.

The active PP stages and their
connections are derived at runtime
from the batch-local PP layout.
end note

note bottom of PPRouting
Autoscaling is represented as PP reconfiguration
where some ranks have empty layer ranges.
Only non-empty ranks are active for new batches.
end note

@enduml

@startuml DynamicPPMigrationSequence
title Runtime PP Reconfiguration / Migration Flow

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 180

actor "Control API / migration_thread" as Control
participant "DynamicEngineCore" as Engine
participant "DynamicScheduler" as Scheduler
participant "DynamicRayDistributedExecutor" as Executor
participant "DynamicGPUWorker" as Worker
participant "KV Synchronizer" as KVSync

Control -> Engine : change_configuration(target_pp_layout)
Engine -> Engine : compare current and target layouts
Engine -> Executor : prepare target layer assignment
Executor -> Worker : load layers needed by target layout
Engine -> Executor : start KV migration plan
Executor -> Worker : install sender/receiver migration state

loop old-layout batches continue
  Engine -> Scheduler : schedule()
  Scheduler --> Engine : batch with old pp_layer_config
  Engine -> Executor : execute(batch)
  Executor -> Worker : forward using batch-local PP layout
  Worker -> KVSync : publish/apply KV patches
end

Engine -> Scheduler : request pending layout switch
Engine -> Scheduler : schedule sync-boundary batch
Scheduler --> Engine : batch with is_sync_after_migration
Scheduler -> Scheduler : update active PP layout to target

Engine -> Executor : execute sync-boundary batch
Executor -> Worker : finalize migration boundary
Worker -> KVSync : ensure all patches applied
Worker -> Worker : cleanup old layers / resize KV if needed
Executor --> Engine : migration finalized

Engine -> Scheduler : resume scheduling with target layout

@enduml
